  {
   "title": "The survivors",
   "body": "Each survivor is an autonomous agent. They perceive only what is near them, choose goals from their needs, personality and ambitions, and pick among several plans for each goal. When a plan fails they learn and try another. They talk, share what they know, ask each other for help, fall in love and fall out. Open their mind from the inspector to see why they act."
  },
  {
   "title": "Influence",
   "body": "You never give orders. Place blueprints (BUILD), set work priorities and policies (COLONY), choose research (RESEARCH), call for expedition volunteers (EXPEDITIONS) and, in Act IV, propose the colony's future. Survivors may refuse, negotiate or find another way."
  },
